DOM XSS via an alternative prototype pollution vector
Information
Category: Prototype Pollution
Difficulty: Practitioner
Status: ✅ Solved
Author: Alejandro Jiménez
Objective

Exploit a client-side prototype pollution vulnerability using an alternative prototype pollution vector to achieve DOM-based Cross-Site Scripting (DOM XSS).

The application allows attacker-controlled URL parameters to modify Object.prototype. A JavaScript gadget then reads the polluted property and passes it to an eval() sink.

The exploitation chain is:

Prototype Pollution
        ↓
Object.prototype.sequence
        ↓
manager.sequence
        ↓
eval()
        ↓
JavaScript execution
        ↓
alert(1)
