DOM XSS
Why the trailing - works

Without the trailing minus character:

alert(1)

is modified by the application to:

alert(1)1

which results in invalid JavaScript syntax.

With the trailing minus:

alert(1)-

the application appends 1:

alert(1)-1

This is syntactically valid JavaScript.

The browser therefore executes:

alert(1)

successfully.

Evidence

The successful exploitation results in the browser displaying:

Alert: 1

This confirms that attacker-controlled JavaScript reached the eval() sink and was executed.

